+A visit's history is a chain of revisions. Each revision is one worker's complete submitted payload, named by a server-assigned revision ID and linked to the revision it started from. At most one revision is a visit's **head** — its current, usable state — at a time; a visit with unresolved review work has no head until a coordinator resolves it.
 
 ## Submission and Retrieval
 
-Authenticate the submitting worker and validate field types and plot references before accepting a submission. Preserve the original payload separately from any later resolved or combined representation. A retry with the same key and identical payload returns the original acceptance result; reuse with a different payload is rejected.
+Authenticate the submitting worker and validate field types and plot references before accepting a submission. Preserve the original payload separately from any later resolved representation. A retry with the same key and identical payload returns the original acceptance result; reuse with a different payload is rejected.
+
+A submission names the revision it started from (its base revision ID, or none for a visit's first submission):
+
+- **Base matches the current head.** The submission becomes the new head. No review work is created.
+- **Base does not match the current head** — another worker's edit landed first from the same base, or the base was itself superseded by an earlier resolution — the submission becomes a **competing revision**: it is stored alongside the current head rather than replacing it, and the visit has no head until a coordinator resolves the competition. This applies uniformly regardless of why the base is stale, so no submitted edit is ever silently dropped for arriving "late."
+
+Current-state retrieval returns the head revision when one exists, and otherwise indicates that the visit has unresolved review work rather than returning a head. Submission-history retrieval returns every revision ever accepted for a visit, including superseded and losing ones.
+
+## Review Resolution
+
+Unresolved review work is the set of competing revisions sharing the same stale base. A coordinator resolves it by selecting one of the competing revisions to become the visit's head; the others remain stored as history but stop competing. The resolution outcome records the coordinator's identity and the full set of competing submission IDs that were in play, alongside which one was selected.
 
-Retrieval must distinguish a usable current state from unresolved review work. Exactly how those states are represented remains part of the open choice.
+A coordinator who judges that none of the competing revisions is correct does not edit one directly — the field worker resubmits a corrected visit through the normal submission path, based on whichever revision the coordinator selected as head. This keeps every stored revision a worker's own submitted payload; the record store never authors visit content.
 
